# ===========================================================================
# MERGE SEMANTICS — the guard-rails that keep an append-only stream append-only
# ===========================================================================
# `corpora/platform-specs/events/quality.jsonl` is an APPEND-ONLY EVENT STREAM.
# Every agent brief in this repo has called it "UNION append-only" for weeks —
# but until 2026-08-15 that rule existed ONLY as discipline: there was no
# `.gitattributes` anywhere in this repo and no merge driver configured, so git
# was 3-way merging an event log as ordinary text.
#
# It had ALREADY diverged three ways when this file was written — `main` 25
# lines, `perf/hosyond-dirty-rows` 7, that checkout's working tree 15 — and a
# trial merge of the reconcile that is coming produced, verbatim:
#
#     CONFLICT (content): Merge conflict in corpora/platform-specs/events/quality.jsonl
#
# i.e. HAND RESOLUTION of an append-only log, which is precisely how events get
# silently dropped. A rule with no mechanism is a rule that is already broken;
# this file is the mechanism.
#
# `union` is a BUILT-IN git merge driver — it takes the lines from BOTH sides
# instead of leaving conflict markers. It needs NO `merge.union.driver` entry in
# git config: defining one would SHADOW the built-in with a custom command and
# is the wrong move. Verified empirically before committing this.
#
# ⛔ SCOPE IS DELIBERATELY NARROW. `union` is correct ONLY where every line is an
# INDEPENDENT append-only record and duplicated or reordered lines are harmless.
# It is SILENT when it is wrong — there is no conflict to notice. The repo's
# other `.jsonl` files (`logs/engineering/*`, `python/logs/*`,
# `intelligence/retrospective/tests/**`, `site/**`) are NOT listed here because
# they have not been assessed against that rule. Widen this only per-file, and
# only after checking that a both-sides merge of that file is meaningful.
# ===========================================================================
corpora/platform-specs/events/quality.jsonl merge=union
